speechtext:
1. At what dates did the Department of Railways approve the completion of new stations, at: (a) Halifax; (b) Hamilton; (c) Vegreville; (d) Wainwright; (e) Salvus?
2. At what dates did the Department of Railways and Canals approve the construction of new stations at: (a) Parry Sound, Ontario;
(b)	Saskatoon; (c) Redbank; (d) Creek des Prairies?

1.	(a) June 6, 1930; (b) December 2, 1930;
(c)	June 6, 1930; (d) September 16, 1930; (e) September 16, 1930.
2.	(a) June 6, 1930; (b) June 6, 1930 (afterwards cancelled); (c) Cancelled; (d) September 16, 1930.

1.	What are the names of: (a) the foreman;
(b)	assistant foreman or supervisor; (c) carpenters; (d) labourers, who have worked in 1931 and who are working on the Riviere du Loup wharf at the present time?
2.	What is the salary of each one of them?
3.	Who recommended them to the department?
Mr. STEWART (Leeds);
1.	Worked on April 10, 1931 (greasing and oiling hoisting apparatus of slips): (a) Alexandre Ouellet, 62i cents per hour; (b) nil;
(c)	nil; (d) Honore Beaulieu, 40 cents per hour, Lucien Potvin, 35 cents per hour, Emile Madore, 35 cents per hour.
At present engaged (improving automobile landing): (a) Alphonse Goulet, $6 per day;
(b)	nil; (c) Alexandre Ouellet, 55 cents per hour, Alfred Pelletier (timberman), 421 cents per hour, Frank Cimon (timberman), 42| cents per hour, Emile Madore (timberman), 42J cents per hour; (d) Guillaume Boucher, 35 cents per hour.
2.	Answered by No. 1.
3.	District engineer.
